# Index of the examples shown in the web interface's gallery, read by
# src/07-user-interface/web/gen_examples/gen_examples.ml to generate the
# module Examples_tpe (see src/07-user-interface/web/dune).
#
# The gallery is a selection: one example per concept, from the simplest to
# the most advanced. The examples under examples/ not listed here vary the
# listed ones over further grading monoids, and are run by tests/examples.t
# with the others.
#
# One example per non-blank, non-comment line, five fields separated by ' | ',
# optionally followed by a sixth and a seventh:
#
#   group | title | grade | path | description
#   group | title | grade | path | description | backend
#   group | title | grade | path | description | backend | settings
#
# - group: the heading of the gallery section the example is listed under.
# - title: the heading of the example's card, without a prefix already given
#   by the group.
# - grade: the grading monoid the web interface switches to when the example
#   is loaded (a key of Grades.GradeRegistry.grade_modules).
# - path: the example's file, relative to this directory.
# - description: one sentence, shown on the example's card.
# - backend: the backend whose gallery lists the example, and which the web
#   interface switches to when it is loaded (a key of BackendRegistry.entries,
#   src/07-user-interface/web/registry); interpreter when not given.
# - settings: the values of inputs of the backend, set when the example is
#   loaded, separated by blanks, each written key=value; the value of a text
#   input is the path of the file holding it, relative to this directory.
#   The inputs not given take their defaults.
#
# Each group is summarised by one line of four fields, the first the word
# 'group', placed before the group's examples:
#
#   group | label | short | summary
#
# - label: the group, as its examples name it.
# - short: the label's short form, shown with the title of the example last
#   loaded on the button that opens the gallery; distinct for distinct groups.
# - summary: one line, shown beside the group's heading.
#
# A group without a summary, or a summary without examples, is an error.
#
# A line of two fields, the first the word 'default', names the example the
# web interface loads when the backend of that example is selected; that of
# the default backend, interpreter, is also loaded when the page is opened:
#
#   default | path
#
# - path: the example's file, relative to this directory, as an example line
#   gives it.
#
# At most one default is given per backend, and one for interpreter.
#
# Examples are listed in the order they appear in the gallery: groups in the
# order given here, and within a group from the simplest example to the most
# advanced.

