group | Introduction | Introduction | Boxes graded first by the time since boxing, then by the operations performed since boxing.
Introduction | Sensor reading | time-interval-rational | introduction/sensor_reading.tpe | A sensor reading in a box graded with a time interval, usable only once its scan is complete and while it is current, with operations taking time and a handler implementing the scan.
Introduction | Stale calibration | regex-upper-bound-rational-symbolic | introduction/stale_calibration.tpe | A sensor calibration in a box graded with a regular expression, usable only if every reconfiguration since calibrating was followed by a self-test.

group | Time grades | Time | Boxes usable after, before or within a duration, whole or fractional.
Time grades | Medication schedule | time-interval-rational | time/intervals_rational.tpe | A medication schedule in hours, whose doses and reports are due within intervals with fractional endpoints, open or closed.
Time grades | Resin printing | time-lower-bound | time/3d_printing.tpe | The stages of a resin print, each boxed for the ticks it has to cool, banked by the printing and curing of the others.

group | Eternal types | Eternal | Values kept across time must have eternal types; a constraint on a type variable becomes a qualifier of the scheme.
Eternal types | Eternal and non-eternal types | time-upper-bound | basics/eternal_types.tpe | Base and algebraic types survive a wait, functions and declared non-eternal types do not, and a polymorphic definition keeps the constraint on its type variable.

group | Effect handlers | Handlers | Operations handled by clauses that respect their grades.
Effect handlers | Lower bounds | time-lower-bound | handlers/lower_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation once it has waited for at least the operation's grade.
Effect handlers | Upper bounds | time-upper-bound | handlers/upper_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation at any point up to the operation's grade, or not at all.
Effect handlers | Nested | time-lower-bound | handlers/nested.tpe | Nested handlers each resume their own continuation, quantifying over one rigid effect per level of nesting.

group | Traces | Traces | Finite sets of traces of operations and delays, exact or with running times.
Traces | Door controller | traces-upper-bound | traces/upper_bounds.tpe | A door controller whose visits are graded by the exact traces they may exhibit, a delay paying for no operation.
Traces | 3D printing | traces-timed-interval | traces_timed_ops/3d_printing.tpe | A print pipeline graded by a lower and an upper bound on its traces, operations counted at their running-time bounds, with eternality constraints on the parts kept across it.

group | Regular expressions | Regex | Regular languages of traces of operations and delays, with and without running times.
Regular expressions | File session | regex-upper-bound-symbolic | regular/upper_bounds.tpe | A file-session and an authentication protocol, each graded by a regular language of operations and ticks.
Regular expressions | Sensor station | regex-timed-upper-bound-symbolic | regular_timed_ops/upper_bounds.tpe | A sensor station graded by regular upper bounds whose ticks pay for operations at their upper running-time bounds.
Regular expressions | Weather station | regex-timed-interval-rational-symbolic | regular_timed_ops/intervals_rational.tpe | A weather station timed in seconds, whose operations declare fractional running-time bounds, one open, and whose windows are regular lower and upper bounds with intervals of durations.
Regular expressions | Mail session | regex-timed-upper-bound-symbolic | regular_timed_ops/mail_session.tpe | A mail session whose retrieval and flagging loops are graded by Kleene stars of traces, with operations taking their declared running times.

group | Rigid order | Rigid | Regular languages whose operations are demanded in order, other operations bought within their delays.
Rigid order | Reaction timer | regex-timed-rigid-upper-bound-rational-symbolic | regular_timed_rigid/upper_bounds_rational.tpe | A reaction timer in milliseconds whose start signal, time stamp and loop of polls are bounded by rigid regular upper bounds, a redraw bought only within a delay that pays for it.

group | Grade lattices | Lattices | Elements of a grade lattice reached, alone or with time bounds and outputs.
Grade lattices | Security levels | lattice | lattice/security.tpe | A box at a security level is out of reach once a higher level has been touched since boxing.
Grade lattices | Expiring capabilities | time-upper-bound-lattice | lattice/time_upper.tpe | A box paired with a time upper bound and an element of the grade lattice: a capability that expires and can be revoked by a taint.
Grade lattices | Flow-sensitive outputs | flow-lattice | lattice/flow.tpe | A report whose public post must come before the vault is read, each output graded by the element reached before it.
Grade lattices | Declared lattice | time-upper-bound-lattice | lattice/quiet_noisy.tpe | A robot step over the declared grade lattice Quiet < Noisy, whose tilt conversion is collected within five ticks and before the motors or the radio are used.

group | Other monoids | Other | Grades beyond time and traces: the levels of resources held, and the counts of operations.
Other monoids | Resource levels | resource-levels | semidirect/resource_levels.tpe | File copies, uploads and log rotations graded by the trough, the net change and the peak of the files and connections they hold.
Other monoids | Rate limits | counts-upper-bound | counts/rate_limits.tpe | A client whose logins and requests are checked against rate limits on each operation.

